GSDM 
Extensible distributed data stream management system 
for scientific applications

The system resides in gsdm subdirectory of Amos II
Subdirectories:
C      C source code including UDP streams
lsp    Lisp source code
osql   Osql source code
dat    Empty directory for storage of report files of execution      
     

1. Installation: create a directory AmosNT under your home directory
and extract the source code from the archive there:
cd AmosNT
unzip gsdm

2. Set environment variables
AMOS_HOME 
   should be set to the name of the directory where Amos II is installed.
NAMESERVER_HOST 
   should be set to the IP address of the machine where the name server will run

3. Compile amos2
Under Windows:
cd bin
install

Under Linux (assuming AmosNT is the directory where the system is unzipped):
cd system/Linux
make
cd ../..


4. Compile GSDM working nodes and coordinator in AmosNT directory:
Under Windows:
gsdminstall

Under Linux:
./gsdminstall_lin

For Linux only: copy startgsdm script into your home directory:
cd ~/
cp AmosNT/startgsdm .

5. Check that you have a valid user account on the servers to be used for GSDM working nodes. Your RSA/DSA public keys (in \.ssh\id_rsa.pub) should also be installed on the server (i.e. appended to ~/.ssh/authorized_keys2 ) in order to avoid entering your password when starting the gsdm servers.

6. Start an example scenario:

a. Start nameserver on the host specified in NAMESERVER_HOST
   amos2 -n NS

b. Start a coordinator server on the same host in subdirectory gsdm:
   amos2 coord.dmp

c. Open the script file in AmosNT/gsdm/osql/start.osql, 
choose a scenario and execute the commands for it in the coordinator. 

d. When the execution stops, you can execute a 'report' command that
creates a text file in gsdm/dat directory with a name composed by the
data flow name, date and time. You can open the file to see the
execution statistics. 

e. Stop the coordinator by:
kill_peer("STATSRV");
quit;

Stop the nameserver by:
^C
quit;


